{"skill":{"slug":"desktop-control","displayName":"Desktop Control"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770255200863,"changelog":"Version 1.0.0\n\n- Initial release of the Desktop Control skill for OpenClaw.\n- Provides advanced automation: mouse movement/clicks, keyboard input, hotkeys, and typing speed control.\n- Supports screen capture, region-based screenshots, image/template matching, and pixel color detection.\n- Includes window management (list, activate, move, resize, minimize/maximize).\n- Safety features: failsafe abort, logging, approval mode, bounds checks, and emergency pause.\n- Detailed documentation with examples and complete API reference.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"ai_agent.py","size":21462,"sha256":"4971f7d14c6e2c0e28999df7ad9f52e65bef4c6a0687e466bd44d5b54ce6d098","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"AI_AGENT_GUIDE.md","size":11051,"sha256":"265239bcc5b43a048282a4f120536c1360d3b1261790efe468dd85228805337c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"demo.py","size":7188,"sha256":"5da659039f391c080778c2208ae7cc0f4a47ae6260d839531d3afb44827a761f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"QUICK_REFERENCE.md","size":5522,"sha256":"a3b817908aea53c6f8f81f6dc2d49429c8db0cb536b4229b556753a1120c460c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":14085,"sha256":"d900c0650cfbb76fcb3a8c156d597ba32ea97b2b87af372315843a251df06b62","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"__init__.py","size":18805,"sha256":"d8f569d4efd3341e631ad46e24412e73ab86b9ba1226ed0d29419093f9da33ae","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2304,"sha256":"6c915053c9df3c51fdc2c88fae8469c5340b716f5824b5a7728abe068ec4551a","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789033549574,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"6ea60cb5f6d243e1bad66dfe9155f1d5693f62ebbeec3be3d5b615bf301455ac","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/6ea60cb5f6d243e1bad66dfe9155f1d5693f62ebbeec3be3d5b615bf301455ac","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\nSuspicious High-Entropy/Eval files: 2\n\nThe skill bundle provides extensive desktop automation capabilities, including full control over mouse, keyboard, screen, window management, clipboard, and the ability to execute commands via the Windows Run dialog (Win+R) in `ai_agent.py`. While these are high-risk capabilities, they are plausibly needed for the stated purpose of 'advanced desktop automation' and the skill includes explicit safety features like failsafe and an approval mode. There is no clear evidence of intentional malicious behavior such as data exfiltration, persistence, or obfuscation. The AI agent's planning is currently rule-based, mitigating immediate prompt injection risk for arbitrary command generation, though the underlying `DesktopController` (in `__init__.py`) offers powerful primitives.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161383461},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":67,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":19,"checkedAt":1789033549574},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This desktop-control skill is coherent, but it needs review because it can control apps, capture screen and clipboard data, and some sensitive actions bypass its advertised approval mode.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill can observe and mutate the active desktop through screenshots, clipboard reads and writes, window focus changes, hotkeys, typing, clicks, drags, and Run-dialog app launch; that authority is broader than the documented safety controls reliably contain.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses ordinary pip packages and I found no remote payload retrieval, but the documented dependency commands are unpinned and do not provide lockfile or hash verification.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The AI agent guide encourages broad natural-language autonomous execution, app launching, form filling, file workflows, and social posting without a clear allowlist, per-action confirmation boundary, or target-app containment.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"I found no startup persistence, service installation, or privilege escalation, but screenshots can be saved to disk and typed or clipboard content is logged, creating persistent exposure of sensitive session data.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The purpose is desktop automation and the main skill text does disclose mouse, keyboard, screen capture, window management, and clipboard operations, but those are high-impact capabilities over the user's full desktop session.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the skill broad control over your current desktop session. Keep failsafe enabled, avoid using it around passwords, tokens, private documents, or sensitive clipboard contents, and treat approval mode as incomplete unless the code is fixed.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Window management, screenshots, and clipboard functions are disclosed in the body of SKILL.md, so this is not hidden tool poisoning by itself; the narrower front-matter description under-discloses some sensitive capabilities.\n[SQP-1] expected: Autonomous interpretation is part of the AI desktop-agent purpose, but the guide presents broad task execution without clear scoping or confirmation requirements for high-impact desktop actions.\n[SQP-2] expected: Screen capture is expected for desktop automation, but the artifacts lack a meaningful privacy warning and ai_agent.py captures before-and-after screenshots for each step by default.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The advertised approval mode does not consistently cover scroll, key_down, key_up, screenshot, clipboard, window activation, or dialog prompt functions, so users may overestimate the consent boundary.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The documentation shows failsafe=False as a performance option and quick reference example without strong warnings despite the skill's ability to send rapid desktop input.\n[SDI-2] expected: Window enumeration and clipboard operations fit a broad desktop-control skill and are documented, but they remain sensitive because they expose or modify session-wide state.\n[SQP-2] expected: Launching applications through Win+R is consistent with app-control automation, but the command can be derived from task text and is not limited by an allowlist beyond a few known app mappings.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding about inconsistent approval enforcement is supported by the code: several sensitive public methods do not call the approval check even when require_approval is enabled.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding about logs is supported: typed text and clipboard content prefixes are included in logger messages and approval prompts.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding about bounds checking is supported: SKILL.md claims bounds checking, while pointer methods pass coordinates directly to PyAutoGUI without validating screen bounds.\n[T08] expected: The dependencies are normal for this purpose, but the install commands use unpinned package names without hash or index constraints.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789033549574}}}}}